        "original_id": "a1c61409-0296-5c43-9bd9-7795e55a71cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Salvia, Arachis, scarlet sage\n- Plant families and taxonomy: Lamiaceae, Fabaceae, Dalbergieae, Pterocarpus clade\n\nFacts:\n- Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the mint family, Lamiaceae.\n- Salvia includes nearly 1000 species of shrubs, herbaceous perennials, and annuals.\n- Arachis is a genus of about 70 species of annual and perennial flowering plants in the pea family, Fabaceae.\n- Arachis is native to South America.\n- Arachis was recently assigned to the informal monophyletic Pterocarpus clade of the Dalbergieae.\n- Scarlet sage may refer to either of two plants in the genus Salvia.",
